 "bound": "the arm set is three scans plus the face on disk; 'published' is therefore the same study at whatever vintage its face was written, so a key that moves between published and a pinned arm may be a vintage difference as well as a population difference -- the pinned arms are the controlled pair and live vs pinned is the population pair; classification is measured from the arms, not from the key's name, so a key whose published value is zero can only ever read 'ratio' (documented per row); E353's summary is derived from E350's rows in the same scan instead of a second walk, and the live arm's pairs is cross-checked against E353's published face rather than assumed equal",
